The simulations use regional model parameters and assume continuous pumping at the maximum allowable rate for the full simulation period, which represents an upper bound on the effects of normal operation. Actual drawdown will depend on the aquifer properties encountered, the constructed well's efficiency and the actual pumping schedule. A post-drilling report presenting the geophysical logs, well completion details, aquifer-test data and water-quality results will be submitted to the District in accordance with Section III of the Guidelines.
